te donovan the  two eventually had a brief relationship  but joshua's arc is mostly remembered  for the incredibly cringe-worthy ways in  which jennifer aniston as rachel tried  to seduce him the writing made it  uncomfortable but there was another  factor at play behind the scenes that  made the relationship even more awkward  aniston and donovan had been a couple in  real life and they'd just broken up when  he got the call to appear on friends he  thought this might be a healthy way to  move past the relationship but he soon  discovered that the opposite was true in  a 2013 interview with huffpost live he  admitted that filming romantic scenes  with his ex was horrible while also  noting i remember just getting back to  my dressing room and just weeping  donovan may have been able to laugh  about it while looking back but it was  clearly a bad experience for him at the  time  charlie sheen isn't exactly known for an  even tempered demeanor he was famously  fired from two and a half men in 2011  following a series of bizarre comments  and behavior and he quickly made enemies  on his follow-up show as well fx decided  that they could make some money with the  sitcom starring sheen so they hired him  for the aptly named anger management  working alongside sheen was selma blair  who played his therapist and part-time  lover kate alas sheen immediately got up  to his old antics including showing up  late and being unprofessional on set  when blair brought the issue up jean  turned on her as one insider told e he  went full throttle into getting her off  the show immediately unsurprisingly for  a charlie sheen vehicle the environment  on set was described as awkward and  toxic for everyone the real kicker was  that blair reportedly found out that she  was fired via text message  sometimes co-stars hit it off right away  only for the relationship to gradually  deteriorate over time but fortunately  nina dobrev and paul wesley experienced  the complete opposite when they starred  together on the vampire diaries dobrev  played elena who was in a love triangle  with paul wesley's stefan and ian  somerhalder's daemon alas dobrev and  wesley clashed immediately they both  stayed quiet about it at the time but  they've talked about it in the years  since during a 2019 appearance on the  directionally challenged podcast for  example dobrev explained there's a fine  line between love and hate and we  despised each other so much that it read  as love  wesley seconded these thoughts in an  interview with entertainment tonight as  he admitted  creatively it just wasn't in sync  thankfully this story has a happy ending  the timeline of the reconciliation is a  little wonky as dobrev says it only took  a few months while wesley claims it took  a few seasons but regardless they  eventually became friends they only have  praise for each other now with both  saying that they talk regularly so now i  just adore her she adores me  pretty much any fan of the x-files knows  that despite mulder and scully's  crackling chemistry on screen the actors  who played them didn't get along  off-screen david duchovny and jillian  anderson played the famous fbi agents on  the fox drama and their characters  eventually went from professional  partners to romantic pair to the delight  of legions of viewers however working  that closely with one other person for  years can lead to some struggles which  duchovny talked about in a 2008  interview with metro at that point he  was able to look back fondly on his time  on the show and even compared anderson  to his sister however he also said that  familiarity breeds contempt and the two  simply got sick of working together  though he insisted that it had nothing  to do with her specifically the intense  shooting schedule and serious subject  matter led to petty arguments and the  company explained that it got to the  point that he and anderson quote  couldn't stand the sight of each other  thankfully this is another story with a  happy ending as the two reunited for an  x-files reboots in 2016 and they'd  clearly gotten past any animosity  particularly if their interview on jimmy  kimmel live from that year is anything  to go by these are people that get along  these two people that i'm looking at  right here  go on  before there was ross and rachel or  mulder and scully tv's ultimate will  they or won't they couple was maddie and  david on moonlighting who were played by  sybil shepard and bruce willis  respectively fans tuned in every week to  see them solve cases and flirt with each  other unfortunately like so many tv  couples with unresolved romantic tension  things quickly went downhill after they  resolved it in 2005 shepard told  entertainment weekly that willis was  great to work with at first as she put  it with bruce the temperature in the  room went 20 degrees higher for me  anyway  however over time the two of them simply  began to hate each other she blamed the  mutual dislike on the show's volatile  nature but their co-star curtis  armstrong has claimed that there was  more to the story as he wrote in his  book revenge of the nerd bruce intimated  to me that there had been one  disastrously ill-conceived thing between  him and sybil early on in the show's run  while not going into explicit details he  made it clear that that kind of mistake  was one i should be sure never to make  fortunately though willis and shepard  eventually decided that their grudge  should die hard with the vengeance and  they even reunited at his comedy central  roast in 2018.  acting alongside someone you've recently  broken up with is one thing but acting  alongside your ex-husband who cheated on  you is another entirely alas that's  exactly what sophia bush had to do on  the teen drama one tree hill she played  brook davis who was in a love triangle  that also involved chad michael murray's  lucas scott at first the romantic  tension between the two boiled over  happily into real life as bush and  murray quickly got engaged and married  but it all came crashing down almost  immediately  the couple said i do in april 2005 but  then they split up in september of that  same year on a 2006 episode of ryan  seacrest's radio show musician nick  carter alleged that this was because his  ex-girlfriend paris hilton had an affair  with murray unfortunately for murray and  bush they had to continue working on one  tree hill together until it came to an  end in 2012. bush has since tried to  avoid talking about the incident but  when it did come up during a 2021  episode of the inside of you podcast she  explained i'm not going to talk about  him i'm not allowed to because i've  tried to poke fun at being a dumb kid  and whenever i've done that it gets  twisted it's not worth my time it's not  a place where i harbor ill will or  anything  similar to mulder and scully richard  castle and kate beckett were  professional partners who also had  fantastic romantic chemistry the castle  leeds eventually became a couple and  started a family as the seasons went on  but the relationship between actors  nathan fillion and stoner katic was  apparently not quite as rosy neither  actor has publicly addressed a working  relationship directly but an insider  told us weekly in 2016 that things were  indeed quite difficult on set phillian  was reportedly so harsh to catic that  she would cry in her dressing room and  the two were apparently even forced to  attend counseling sessions together the  show ended in 2016 after eight seasons  but her departure from it was quite  messy first it was announced that her  contract hadn't been renewed and then  abc announced that the show was ending  in a 2018 interview with entertainment  weekly katic addressed her departure by  noting it hurt and it was a harsh ending  however she did also claim that she was  still overall thankful for the  experience  sitcoms wouldn't be what they are today  without i love lucy lucille ball was of  course the star of the show but her  co-stars vivian vance and william  frawley who played lucy's neighbors  ethel and fred mertz were also a big  part of what made it so great the always  bickering couple had fantastic chemistry  but the fighting didn't end when the  camera stopped rolling  vance was only two years younger than  ball but she was playing the wife of a  man more than two decades her senior  according to the book meet the mertes  fans admitted i loathed william frawley  and the feeling was mutual whenever i  received a new script i raced through it  praying that there wouldn't be a scene  where we had to be in bed together  frawley in turn didn't have very nice  things to say as he quipped she's one of  the finest girls to come out of kansas  but i often wish she'd go back there  according to an oft-repeated story which  was recorded in the book the dead  celebrity cookbook vance was at a  restaurant when she learned that frawley  had died upon hearing the news she  ordered champagne for everyone whether  or not this story is true it accurately  sums up the hostile working relationship  between the two  martin lawrence is no stranger to  controversy his infamous saturday night  live monologue in 1994 reportedly got  him a lifetime ban from the show for  example his sitcom martin which ran on  fox from 1992 to 1997 was popular but  also not without controversy a big  reason for the show's success was  lawrence's chemistry with tasha campbell  who played his wife gina alas things  were much rockier when the cameras  weren't rolling campbell left the show  in the fifth season and brought legal  action against lawrence for repeated and  escalating sexual harassment sexual  battery verbal abuse and related threats  the case was ultimately settled out of  court and campbell returned for the  show's finale however since lawrence  wasn't allowed to be around her when she  shot her scenes it made for an awkward  conclusion in the 2020 interview with gq  lawrence claimed that the sexual  harassment quote didn't happen meanwhile  campbell revealed on an episode of the  talk that same year that due to the  settlement agreement she isn't allowed  to speak about the matter in much detail  if you or anyone you know has been a  victim of sexual assault help is  available visit the rape abused and  incest national network website or  contact reigns national helpline at  1-800-656-hope 1-800-656-4673  [Music]  you

